  <h1>Chromatron</h1>

  <p>Original game by <a href="https://www.silverspaceship.com/chromatron/">Silver Spaceship Software</a>.<br>
  Recompiled binaries posted with the original author's permission.<br>
  Recompilation by <a href="https://p.migdal.pl/">Piotr Migda&#x142;</a> (blog post coming soon).</p>

  <h2>Play in Browser</h2>
  <p><a class="play-btn" href="play/">&#9654; Play Chromatron</a></p>

  <h2>Download</h2>
  <h3>macOS</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/__DIST_REPO__/releases/latest/download/Chromatron-macos-apple-silicon-unsigned.dmg">macOS Apple Silicon (.dmg)</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/__DIST_REPO__/releases/latest/download/Chromatron-macos-intel-unsigned.dmg">macOS Intel (.dmg)</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Windows</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/__DIST_REPO__/releases/latest/download/Chromatron-windows-x86_64.zip">Windows x86_64 (.zip)</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Linux</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/__DIST_REPO__/releases/latest/download/Chromatron-linux-x86_64.tar.gz">Linux x86_64 (.tar.gz)</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Installation Notes</h2>
  <h3>macOS</h3>
  <p>If you get a message saying the app is damaged and cannot be opened, run in Terminal:</p>
  <pre><code>xattr -cr /Applications/Chromatron.app</code></pre>
  <p>This is necessary because the app is not signed with an Apple Developer ID.</p>

  <h3>Windows</h3>
  <p>Extract the zip and run <code>chromatron.exe</code>. Windows SmartScreen may warn about an unrecognized app &mdash; click &ldquo;More info&rdquo; then &ldquo;Run anyway&rdquo;.</p>

  <h3>Linux</h3>
  <p>Extract and run:</p>
  <pre><code>tar xzf Chromatron-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
chmod +x chromatron
./chromatron</code></pre>

